To retrieve a service account key file in Google Cloud, follow these steps:

Go to the Google Cloud Console:
https://console.cloud.google.com/welcome?project=cohesive-amp-433406-b0

Open your browser and navigate to the Google Cloud Console.
Select your project:

At the top of the page, select the project for which you want to generate a service account key.
Navigate to IAM & Admin:

On the left sidebar, go to IAM & Admin and then select Service Accounts.
Create a new service account (if needed):

If you don’t have a service account already, click on + CREATE SERVICE ACCOUNT.
Enter a name for the service account, e.g., "my-service-account".
Choose roles that suit your needs and click Continue.
Click Done after creating the service account.
Generate a key for the service account:

Find the service account you want to use in the list.
Click on the Actions (three vertical dots) menu next to the service account and select Manage keys.
Click on Add Key and then Create new key.
Select JSON as the key type and click Create.
A JSON key file will be downloaded to your computer.
Save the key file:

Keep this file secure as it contains sensitive information.
Use the key file in your application:

This JSON file contains the information you need to authenticate your application, similar to the data you posted.